 area of a circle is calculated using the formula \( A = \pi r^2 \). Plugging in the radius of 5 units:\( A = \pi (5)^2 = \pi 	imes 25 = 25\pi \) square units. # 2. Dataset 12345&lt;|User|&gt;Can you explain what gravity is in simple terms?&lt;|Assistant|&gt;Absolutely! Gravity is a force that pulls objects toward each other. # 3. Dataset 1234567891011121314151617# Code from https://github.com/rasbt/LLMs-from-scratch/blob/main/ch07/01_main-chapter-code/ch07.ipynbdef format_input(entry): instruction_text = ( f&quot;Below is an instruction that describes a task. &quot; f&quot;Write a response that appropriately completes the request.&quot; f&quot;

