来源路径： 02-知识点/防御检测与OPSEC/macOS NVRAM 技术笔记.md 自动导入：安全知识库笔记，已对示例密钥 / Token 做公开发布脱敏。 # macOS NVRAM 技术笔记 [!summary] 提炼定位 面向 防御检测与 OPSEC 的知识点；已剥离原仓库目录、构建说明、站点资产和安装噪声，只保留概念、流程、命令、工具、方法论与检测线索。 # 适用场景 围绕 macOS NVRAM 技术笔记 建立检测、规避、溯源或 OPSEC 检查。 把行为、进程链、网络、文件、日志事件转化为可验证线索。 # 中文提炼 核心目标是围绕 macOS NVRAM 技术笔记 建立行为证据、检测逻辑和操作暴露面。 优先关注：macOS NVRAM、Basic Information、NVRAM Access from User Space、Reading NVRAM、Writing NVRAM；把命令、进程、文件、网络、注册表 / 日志事件映射到检测字段。 区分正常管理行为与攻击行为，避免只按工具名告警；优先写可复现的查询条件。 OPSEC 记录应包括噪声来源、持久化痕迹、清理步骤和不可规避风险。 本页已沉淀 8 组命令 / 载荷片段；使用时先核对授权范围、目标环境和副作用。 # 关键主题 macOS NVRAM Basic Information NVRAM Access from User Space Reading NVRAM Writing NVRAM CS NVRAM UNRESTRICTED Flag Finding NVRAM-Unrestricted Binaries Security Implications Weakening SIP via NVRAM Enabling Kernel Debugging Firmware 持久化 AMFI 绕过 Real-World CVEs 枚举 Script # 核心要点 Writing NVRAM variables requires root privileges and, for system-critical variables (like csr-active-config), the process must have specific code-signing flags or entitlements: If an attacker can write to NVRAM (either through a compromised NVRAM-unrestricted binary or by exploiting a 漏洞), they can modify csr-active-config to disable SIP protections on next boot: NVRAM modifications survive OS reinstallation — they persist at the firmware level. An attacker can write custom NVRAM variables that a 持久化 mechanism reads at boot: NVRAM 持久化 survives disk wipes and OS reinstalls. It requires PRAM/NVRAM reset (Command+Option+P+R on Intel Macs) or DFU restore (Apple Silicon) to clear. The amfi get out of my way=1 boot argument disables Apple Mobile File Integrity, allowing unsigned code to execute: # 命令 / 载荷 / 操作片段 # 1. Reading NVRAM 123456789101112# List all NVRAM variablesnvram -p# Read a specific variablenvram boot-args# Export all NVRAM as XML plistnvram -xp# Read SIP configurationnvram csr-active-configcsrutil status # 2. Writing NVRAM 12345678# Set boot-args (requires root)sudo nvram boot-args=&quot;debug=0x144 kcsuffix=development&quot;# Clear boot-argssudo nvram -d boot-args# Set a custom variablesudo nvram MyCustomVar=&quot;persistence-value&quot; # 3. Finding NVRAM-Unrestricted Binaries 12# Check code signing flags for a binarycodesign -dvvv /usr/sbin/nvram 2&gt;&amp;1 | grep &quot;flags=&quot; # 4. Weakening SIP via NVRAM 12345678910111213141516# SIP configuration is a bitmask stored in NVRAM# Each bit controls a different SIP protection:# Bit 0 (0x1): Filesystem protection# Bit 1 (0x2): Kext signing# Bit 2 (0x4): Task-for-pid restriction# Bit 3 (0x8): Unrestricted filesystem# Bit 4 (0x10): Apple Internal (debug)# Bit 5 (0x20): Unrestricted DTrace# Bit 6 (0x40): Unrestricted NVRAM# Bit 7 (0x80): Device configuration# Current SIP configurationnvram csr-active-config | xxd# On older hardware, a compromised NVRAM-unrestricted binary could:# nvram csr-active-config=%7f%00%00%00 # Disable most SIP protections # 5. Enabling Kernel Debugging 1234567891011# Enable kernel debug flags via boot-argssudo nvram boot-args=&quot;debug=0x144&quot;# Common debug flags:# 0x01 DB_HALT — Wait for debugger at boot# 0x04 DB_KPRT — Send kernel printf to serial# 0x40 DB_KERN_DUMP — Dump kernel core on NMI# 0x100 DB_REBOOT_POST_PANIC — Reboot after panic# Use development kernelsudo nvram boot-args=&quot;kcsuffix=development&quot; # 6. Firmware 持久化 12345# Write a persistence markernvram attacker-payload-config=&quot;base64_encoded_config_here&quot;# A startup script or LaunchDaemon could read this:nvram attacker-payload-config 2&gt;/dev/null &amp;&amp; /path/to/payload # 7. AMFI 绕过 12# This requires NVRAM write access AND reduced security boot:sudo nvram boot-args=&quot;amfi_get_out_of_my_way=1&quot; # 8. 枚举 Script 12345678910111213141516171819202122232425#!/bin/bashecho &quot;=== NVRAM Security Audit ===&quot;# Current SIP statusecho -e &quot;
[*] SIP Status:&quot;csrutil status# Current boot-argsecho -e &quot;
[*] Boot Arguments:&quot;nvram boot-args 2&gt;/dev/null || echo &quot; (none set)&quot;# All NVRAM variablesecho -e &quot;
[*] All NVRAM Variables:&quot;nvram -p | grep -v &quot;^$&quot; | wc -lecho &quot; variables total&quot;# Security-relevant variablesecho -e &quot;
[*] Security-Relevant Variables:&quot;for var in csr-active-config boot-args StartupMute SystemAudioVolume efi-boot-device; do echo &quot; $var: $(nvram &quot;$var&quot; 2&gt;/dev/null || echo &#x27;not set&#x27;)&quot;done# Check for custom (non-Apple) variablesecho -e &quot;
[*] Non-Standard Variables (potential persistence):&quot;nvram -p | grep -v &quot;^$&quot; | grep -vE &quot;^(SystemAudioVolume|boot-args|csr-active-config|prev-lang|LocationServicesEnabled|fmm-mobileme-token|bluetoothInternalControllerAddress|bluetoothActiveControllerInfo|SystemAudioVolumeExtension|efi-)&quot; | head -20 # 工具与参考入口 Apple Platform Security Guide — Boot process Apple Security Updates — NVRAM-related CVEs Duo Labs — Apple T2 Security # 检查清单 是否提取进程链 / 命令行 / 网络 / 文件 / 日志线索 是否区分攻击行为和正常管理行为 是否记录绕过假设与限制 是否形成检测规则或查询语句 # 关联 防御检测与 OPSEC 总览 知识地图 # 扩展记录 可在这里补充

